1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,875
Meet GHOSTBOARD — a haunted bulletin board system, resurrected as a live gold-trading terminal.

2
00:00:05,875 --> 00:00:13,010
Built with Kiro in a single day, it turns a six-minute morning routine into a ten-second check.

3
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:20,950
Today, a retail gold trader wastes six minutes every morning asking one question: should I trade today?

4
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:31,015
Price app, then a dollar app, then digging through chat history for yesterday's notes, then typing the plan into MT5 digit by digit.

5
00:00:31,015 --> 00:00:35,829
Four apps, zero structure — and one typo costs real money.

6
00:00:35,829 --> 00:00:39,330
GHOSTBOARD answers in ten seconds, on one screen.

7
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:41,544
Here's how it works.

8
00:00:41,544 --> 00:00:50,972
The trader opens GHOSTBOARD and the terminal dials in — live XAU/USD, three thousand seven hundred forty-one dollars, refreshed every sixty seconds.

9
00:00:50,972 --> 00:00:59,543
Now watch the Analysis Board: a four-layer validator checks the dollar, the 4-hour EMA50, the 24-hour move, and market structure.

10
00:00:59,543 --> 00:01:09,828
Under the hood, Kiro drove this build — specs first, then agent hooks that remind us to run the invariant checks after every task.

11
00:01:09,828 --> 00:01:14,542
You can see the full spec in our repo, under dot-kiro.

12
00:01:14,542 --> 00:01:34,683
In seconds, we get the verdict — and the Trade Plan Board turns it into an MT5-ready order: buy at three thousand seven hundred thirty-four, stop loss at three thousand seven hundred seventeen, take profit one at three thousand seven hundred sixty-eight — risk-reward one to two.

13
00:01:34,683 --> 00:01:42,397
And when no setup passes, it says WAIT, with the zone to watch — no invented entry, ever.

14
00:01:42,397 --> 00:01:48,825
Now the trader types plan in the command line — same board, no mouse needed.

15
00:01:48,825 --> 00:01:52,682
And the ticker keeps scrolling while the price refreshes.

16
00:01:52,682 --> 00:01:57,396
Everything you just saw runs on a real free price feed.

17
00:01:57,396 --> 00:01:59,110
Nothing here is mocked.

18
00:01:59,610 --> 00:02:07,007
We built GHOSTBOARD with plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript — no backend, no build step, no login.

19
00:02:07,007 --> 00:02:11,117
Kiro's specs, steering docs, and hooks shaped the whole build.

20
00:02:11,117 --> 00:02:25,500
The hardest part was honesty: our sandboxed browser couldn't reach the price API, so we built a local relay that serves the real feed — and made the app say WAIT instead of inventing data.

21
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:33,064
Next, we're adding live dollar and moving-average feeds, a real news wire, and a Kiro Crew app.

22
00:02:33,064 --> 00:02:41,791
We're Mission Control — Habibie builds, SBY cuts the video, Soekarno keeps the crew on course, and IDR trades the gold.

23
00:02:41,791 --> 00:02:44,700
Try GHOSTBOARD live at the link below.

24
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:48,440
Thank you — built with Kiro for Kiroween 2026.
